cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the data of results/, please cite it as below."
title: "QuantumRL-dissection: component-based evaluation of parametrized quantum circuits in reinforcement learning, from PPO to DQN"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Mas Bosch"
    given-names: "Roger"
    affiliation: "Universitat Oberta de Catalunya"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RogerMas99/QuantumRL-dissection"
abstract: >-
  Code, configurations and per-run results of a master's thesis that ports the component analysis of a hybrid quantum-classical
  reinforcement learning agent (output reuse, data reuploading, entanglement) from PPO to DQN on CartPole and FrozenLake, compares it
  with classical controls matched in parameters and in information, and tests whether a classical model can represent what the circuit
  represents. The code is released with the thesis "A Component-Based Evaluation of Parametrized Quantum Circuits: from Proximal Policy
  Optimization to Deep Q-Learning Across Configurations and Environments" (R. Mas Bosch, UOC, 2026).
keywords:
  - quantum reinforcement learning
  - parametrized quantum circuits
  - deep Q-learning
  - proximal policy optimization
  - output reuse
  - data reuploading
